  "lineage": "Pasibutbut is the Bunun prayer for a good millet harvest, sung by a circle of men in the millet-planting season; voices in four parts start low and rise gradually, each singer adjusting to the others, and the overtones of the ascending chord led to its Taiwanese description as 'eight-part harmony'. Kurosawa Takatomo recorded it in 1943.",
